From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cfg80211: assert the wiphy lock only for concurrent DFS lookup

The ordinary channel-availability path can reject concurrent DFS from static
feature, channel and interface attributes without walking interface state.
Require the wiphy lock where the concurrent BSS lookup actually needs it,
so callers without concurrent DFS keep their existing lockless query path.

Not submitted upstream.

Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
---
--- a/net/wireless/chan.c
+++ b/net/wireless/chan.c
@@ -966,8 +966,6 @@
 	struct wireless_dev *wdev;
 	struct cfg80211_registered_device *rdev = wiphy_to_rdev(wiphy);
 
-	lockdep_assert_held(&rdev->wiphy.mtx);
-
 	if (!wiphy_ext_feature_isset(&rdev->wiphy,
 				     NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_DFS_CONCURRENT) ||
 	    !(chan->flags & IEEE80211_CHAN_DFS_CONCURRENT))
@@ -976,6 +974,8 @@
 	/* only valid for P2P GO */
 	if (iftype != NL80211_IFTYPE_P2P_GO)
 		return false;
+
+	lockdep_assert_held(&rdev->wiphy.mtx);
 
 	/*
 	 * Allow only if there's a concurrent BSS
